IMPORT prelude

-- Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990 (Singapore) -- the foreign employee's questions about one work pass and one
-- employment: whether the Act treats me as a foreigner, a foreign employee or a self-employed foreigner (s 2); whether
-- my work pass is valid for the work I do (s 12, with reg 2(3) of the Work Passes Regulations); whether I commit an
-- offence by working (ss 5(2), 10) and what I can be punished with (ss 5(7), 10(2), 22); whether I can be arrested
-- without a warrant and for how long I can be held (s 21); what my employer may and may not take from me (ss 22A,
-- 25(4), 25(6), with regs 17 and 18 and the Seventh Schedule) and what the court must order if it convicts the taker
-- (s 23A); what happens to my employment when my pass is suspended or revoked (s 9); the levy on my pass (s 11);
-- reporting a lost pass (s 14); what the person who employs me risks by employing me unlawfully (ss 5(4)-(6), (8),
-- 6, 6A, 9(3), 22A(2), 22B, 25(1)-(4), 25A); the financial penalties the Controller can impose on me and my appeal (ss 25(2), 25A, 25C,
-- 25G); and composition (s 27).
--
-- SEAT: the foreign employee -- a foreigner who works, or seeks or is offered work, in Singapore for an employer
-- (and, for s 10 and s 11, the foreigner who works on his or her own account). One case is one work pass and one
-- employment. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it, from facts that person could state. Where the
-- Act speaks to the employer, the occupier, the Controller or the court, what is encoded is what that means for me.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EFMA1990.txt; and the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012
-- (S 569/2012), informal consolidation in force from 1/1/2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EFMA1990-S569-2012.txt (regs 2(3), 17, 18 and the Seventh Schedule only).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Appointments and the Controller's status (ss 3, 3A), exemptions (s 4), the Controller's application,
-- renewal and debarment powers (s 7, except as inputs), the employer's register (s 8), cancellation on the employer's
-- application (s 9(2), (4)), burden of proof (s 15), inspection, change of address, service and protection (ss 16-19),
-- offences by bodies corporate (s 20), the manner of arrest and its incidents (ss 21A-21G), abetment (ss 23, 25F),
-- complaints (s 24), the detail of the employer-only infringements (s 25(1), (3), (5); maxima only), directions
-- (s 25B), recovery of
-- penalties (s 25D), bodies corporate (s 25E), the Appeal Board's constitution (s 25H), courts, forms, regulations
-- and transitional provisions (ss 26, 28-30), and the Schedule (personal identifiers). From the Regulations, every
-- work pass condition (First to Sixth Schedules, including the Fourth Schedule Parts VI and VII conditions that bind
-- the worker), security, fees other than the duplicate-pass fees, and reg 20. The levy rates and the late-payment
-- rate are set by order under s 11, not deposited: they are inputs.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the foreign
-- employee, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990 -- the foreign employee's questions`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- am I a foreigner, a foreign employee or a self-employed foreigner`

-- "foreigner" means "any person who is not a citizen of Singapore or permanent resident of Singapore".
-- "foreign employee" means "(a) any foreigner, other than a self-employed foreigner, who seeks or is offered
-- employment in Singapore; or (b) any other person or class of persons as the Minister may, by notification in the
-- Gazette, specify".
-- "self-employed foreigner" means "any foreigner who, not being employed under a contract of service, seeks to engage
-- in or engages in -- (a) any trade, vocation or profession, whether for the purpose of gain or otherwise; or (b) any
-- other activity in Singapore for the purpose of gain".
-- "employ" means "to engage or use the service of any person for the purpose of -- (a) any work; or (b) providing any
-- training for that person, whether under a contract of service or otherwise, and with or without salary".
-- Gloss: a "work pass" is the permit, S pass, employment pass or other pass the Controller of Work Passes issues; a
-- "contract of service" is an employment contract (as against working for oneself).
DECLARE `Standing` IS ONE OF
    `a citizen of Singapore`
    `a permanent resident of Singapore`
    `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident`

DECLARE `Me` HAS
    `my standing`                                                                  IS A `Standing`
    -- INFERENCE: a person already at work for an employer "is offered employment"; asked as one fact.
    `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am employed under a contract of service`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I engage or seek to engage in a trade, vocation or profession`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I engage or seek to engage in another activity in Singapore for gain`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Conditional on an official act: the Minister's Gazette notification under limb (b).
    `the Minister has specified by Gazette notification a class I belong to as foreign employees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foreigner under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `me`'s `my standing`
    WHEN `neither a citizen nor a permanent resident` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a self-employed foreigner` IF
        `Am I a foreigner under the Act` `me`
    AND NOT `me`'s `I am employed under a contract of service`
    AND (    `me`'s `I engage or seek to engage in a trade, vocation or profession`
         OR  `me`'s `I engage or seek to engage in another activity in Singapore for gain`)

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foreign employee` IF
        (    `Am I a foreigner under the Act` `me`
         AND NOT `Am I a self-employed foreigner` `me`
         AND `me`'s `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore`)
    OR  `me`'s `the Minister has specified by Gazette notification a class I belong to as foreign employees`

§§ `12 -- is my work pass valid for this work`

-- s 12(1): "A work pass for a foreign employee is valid only in respect of the employer and the foreign employee
-- specified in the work pass, and -- (a) the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment -- (i) that is
-- specified in the work pass; or (ii) in any other case, that was submitted to the Controller in, or in connection
-- with, the application for the work pass; and (b) any trade, sector, occupation or type of employment not specified
-- in the work pass, for which the foreign employee has the Controller's approval to engage in."
-- s 12(2) says the same for a self-employed foreigner's "trade, sector, vocation, profession or activity".
-- s 12(3): "valid for the period specified in the work pass unless it is earlier suspended or revoked by the
-- Controller, or earlier cancelled by the Controller on the application by the employer or self-employed foreigner".
-- Regulations, reg 2(3): where my pass from the Controller of Immigration "expires and is not renewed or is
-- cancelled", my work pass "shall by the operation of this regulation also cease to be valid".
-- Gloss: the "Controller" is the Controller of Work Passes, the official who issues and revokes passes.
DECLARE `My work pass` HAS
    `I hold a work pass issued to me`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pass names as my employer the person I work for`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Conditional on an official act: the Controller's approval under s 12(1)(b).
    `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period specified in the pass has not ended`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled`            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pass is still in force` IF
        `pass`'s `I hold a work pass issued to me`
    AND `pass`'s `the period specified in the pass has not ended`
    AND NOT `pass`'s `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass`
    AND NOT `pass`'s `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application`
    AND NOT `pass`'s `my immigration pass has expired without renewal or been cancelled`

GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` IF
        `the pass is still in force` `pass`
    AND `pass`'s `the pass names as my employer the person I work for`
    AND (    `pass`'s `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application`
         OR  `pass`'s `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work`)

GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work pass valid for the activity I carry on for myself` IF
        `the pass is still in force` `pass`
    AND (    `pass`'s `the work is in the trade, sector, occupation or type of employment specified in the pass or submitted in the application`
         OR  `pass`'s `if the Controller has approved me to engage in this other work`)

§§ `5(2), 10(1) -- am I committing an offence by working`

-- s 5(2): "A foreign employee must not be in the employment of an employer without a valid work pass."
-- s 10(1): "A foreigner must not be a self-employed foreigner unless he or she has a valid work pass."
-- "valid work pass" means "a work pass that is valid in accordance with section 12".
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`, `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I breaking section 5(2) by working for this employer` IF
        `Am I a foreign employee` `me`
    AND `me`'s `I seek, have been offered or am in employment in Singapore`
    AND NOT `Is my work pass valid for this work for this employer` `pass`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`, `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I breaking section 10(1) by working for myself` IF
        `Am I a self-employed foreigner` `me`
    AND NOT `Is my work pass valid for the activity I carry on for myself` `pass`

§§ `5(7), 10(2), 13, 14, 22 -- what I can be punished with`

-- s 5(7): contravening s 5(2) -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or
-- to both".
-- s 10(2): "(a) ... a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both; and
-- (b) on a second or subsequent conviction, be punished with imprisonment for a term of not less than one month and
-- not more than 2 years and also be liable to a fine not exceeding $20,000".
-- s 22(1): (a) contravening "any condition (other than a regulatory condition)" of the pass; (b) not producing the
-- pass "upon demand" (s 13(4)); (c) "wilfully obstructs" an officer; (d) a statement "which the person knows, or ought
-- reasonably to know, is false in any material particular"; (e) "sells, forges, unlawfully alters or, without lawful
-- authority, transfers or allows another person to use" a pass; (f) "uses or, without lawful authority, has in the
-- person's possession" a forged pass or one "issued to another person"; (g) contravenes s 13(1) (letting another
-- person possess my pass), 13(2) (handing it to my employer on my last day, "If required by the Controller") or 14
-- (reporting loss "within 7 days"). Punishment: (h) for (a)-(c) "$10,000 or ... 12 months or ... both"; (i) for
-- (d)-(f) "$20,000 or ... 2 years or ... both"; (j) for (g) "a fine not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 22(2): knowing of a (1)(d) offence and "intentionally omits to provide any information to the Controller" --
-- $10,000 or 12 months or both. s 22(3): a false statement "relating to his or her qualifications" -- $20,000 or 2
-- years or both.
-- Gloss: "or to both" lets the court impose a fine, prison or both; a mandatory minimum binds it.
DECLARE `My offence` IS ONE OF
    `being in employment without a valid work pass`
    `being a self-employed foreigner without a valid work pass`
    `contravening a condition of my work pass that is not a regulatory condition`
    `not producing my work pass on demand`
    `wilfully obstructing an officer or employment inspector`
    `giving the Controller information I know or ought to know is false`
    `selling, forging, altering or letting another person use a work pass`
    `using a forged work pass or one issued to another person`
    `letting another person have possession of my work pass`
    `not handing my work pass to my employer on my last day when required`
    `not reporting the loss of my work pass within 7 days`
    `not telling the Controller of a false statement I know was made`
    `making a false statement about my qualifications`

DECLARE `Punishment` HAS
    `the least fine`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the most fine`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the least months of imprisonment`   IS A NUMBER
    `the most months of imprisonment`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `lo` IS A NUMBER, `hi` IS A NUMBER, `plo` IS A NUMBER, `phi` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Punishment`
`a fine from` MEANS
    `Punishment` WITH
        `the least fine`                   IS `lo`
        `the most fine`                    IS `hi`
        `the least months of imprisonment` IS `plo`
        `the most months of imprisonment`  IS `phi`

-- The table, as the Act states it: least fine, most fine, least months, most months.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Punishment`
`the punishment the Act sets for my offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `being in employment without a valid work pass`                           THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24
    WHEN `being a self-employed foreigner without a valid work pass`               THEN
        IF `this is a second or subsequent conviction`
        THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 1 24
        ELSE `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24
    WHEN `contravening a condition of my work pass that is not a regulatory condition` THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 12
    WHEN `not producing my work pass on demand`                                    THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 12
    WHEN `wilfully obstructing an officer or employment inspector`                 THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 12
    WHEN `giving the Controller information I know or ought to know is false`      THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24
    WHEN `selling, forging, altering or letting another person use a work pass`    THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24
    WHEN `using a forged work pass or one issued to another person`                THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24
    WHEN `letting another person have possession of my work pass`                  THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 0
    WHEN `not handing my work pass to my employer on my last day when required`    THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 0
    WHEN `not reporting the loss of my work pass within 7 days`                    THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 0
    WHEN `not telling the Controller of a false statement I know was made`         THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 12
    WHEN `making a false statement about my qualifications`                        THEN `a fine from` 0 20000 0 24

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined for` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for my offence` `the offence` `this is a second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the most fine`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for my offence` `the offence` `this is a second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the most months of imprisonment`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the shortest imprisonment I must get, in months` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for my offence` `the offence` `this is a second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the least months of imprisonment`

-- s 27(1): the Controller may compound an offence by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) a sum of $5,000."
-- Gloss: to "compound" is to settle the offence for a payment; s 27(3): "no further proceedings are to be taken".
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can cost for an offence whose maximum fine is` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`, `this is a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound my offence` MEANS
    `the most a composition can cost for an offence whose maximum fine is` (`What is the most I can be fined for` `the offence` `this is a second or subsequent conviction`)

§§ `21 -- can I be arrested without a warrant, and for how long can I be held`

-- s 21(1): "Any police officer or employment inspector may arrest without warrant any person whom he or she
-- reasonably suspects -- (a) is committing or has committed an offence under section 5(6), (7) or (8), 10(2),
-- 22(1)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f), (2), (3) or (4), 22A(2) or 22B(1)". Not listed: s 22(1)(b) and (g).
-- s 21(4): an employment inspector "must not detain in custody a person arrested without warrant for longer than is
-- reasonable in the circumstances, and such period must not exceed 48 hours (excluding the time necessary for the
-- journey from the place of arrest to the Magistrate's Court)".
-- Gloss: an "employment inspector" is an officer appointed under s 3 to enforce the Act.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `My offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be arrested without a warrant if suspected of` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not producing my work pass on demand`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `letting another person have possession of my work pass`               THEN FALSE
    WHEN `not handing my work pass to my employer on my last day when required` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `not reporting the loss of my work pass within 7 days`                 THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The 48-hour limit binds an employment inspector; arrests by a police officer fall under the Criminal Procedure
-- Code 2010, not deposited, so the encoding says it does not decide them.
DECLARE `Who arrested me` IS ONE OF `an employment inspector`, `a police officer`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who arrested me`, `hours held, not counting the journey to the Magistrate's Court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Have I been held longer than the Act allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `an employment inspector` THEN JUST (`hours held, not counting the journey to the Magistrate's Court` GREATER THAN 48)
    WHEN `a police officer`        THEN NOTHING

§§ `22A, 23A, 25(4), 25(6) -- what my employer may take from me`

-- s 22A(1): a person "must not deduct from any salary payable to a foreign employee, or demand or receive, directly or
-- indirectly and whether in Singapore or elsewhere, from a foreign employee any sum or other benefit -- (a) as
-- consideration or as a condition for the employment ...; (b) as consideration or as a condition for the continued
-- employment ...; or (c) as a financial guarantee related, in any way, to the employment". (2): fine up to $30,000 or 2
-- years or both.
-- s 22A(3): any other sum taken "is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have done so as consideration for the
-- employment", unless it is (a) an amount "that the employer of the foreign employee must bear and is liable to pay
-- under section 25(6)"; (b) a fee "prescribed as recoverable from the foreign employee under section 25(6)(a)"; (c)/(d)
-- a deduction the Employment Act 1968 ss 26 to 32 authorise, or where they do not apply one "made in accordance with
-- the terms of the employment"; (e) a fee an Employment Agencies Act 1958 licensee "may lawfully charge".
-- s 25(6): "the employer of a foreign employee shall, except where the Controller permits otherwise, bear and be liable
-- to pay": (a) pass application, issuance, renewal or reinstatement fees, "other than the fees or deductions prescribed
-- as recoverable from the foreign employee"; (b) security; (c) medical insurance; (d) medical examinations; (e) "the
-- levy ... and any penalty due thereon"; (f) training "required by the employer or the Controller"; (g) "repatriating
-- the foreign employee at any time"; (h) anything prescribed. s 25(4): an employer who takes any of these from me, or
-- causes me to bear them, may be given "a financial penalty of an amount, not exceeding $20,000".
-- Regulations, reg 17: "For the purposes of section 25(6)(a) of the Act, the Controller permits an employer to recover"
-- the duplicate-pass fees for a damaged pass and for the FIRST replacement of a lost pass (Seventh Schedule items
-- 1(e), (f); 2(d), (e); 3(d), (e); 4(c), (d); 8(b), (c) and others) "if the damage to or loss of the foreign
-- employee's [pass] was caused by the negligence of the foreign employee". The fee for a second or later lost pass
-- (1(g), 2(f), 3(f), 4(e), 8(d)) is not listed. The miscellaneous work pass has no duplicate-pass fee.
-- Regulations, reg 18: for an S pass, employment pass, personalised employment pass, work holiday pass or
-- miscellaneous work pass, the employer bears training it requires and repatriation "except the Controller permits the
-- foreign employee bearing such costs if the foreign employee consents in writing to bear such costs".
-- Gloss: the "levy" is the monthly charge the Minister imposes by order for holding a work pass (s 11).
DECLARE `Kind of work pass` IS ONE OF
    `a work permit for a domestic worker`
    `a work permit for other work`
    `an S pass`
    `an employment pass`
    `a personalised employment pass`
    `a work holiday pass`
    `a miscellaneous work pass`

DECLARE `Charge` IS ONE OF
    `a fee for getting the job`
    `a fee for keeping the job`
    `a deposit or other financial guarantee for my employment`
    `work pass application, issue, renewal or reinstatement fees`
    `the cost of security the Controller requires`
    `my medical insurance the Controller requires`
    `my medical examinations the Controller requires`
    `the levy or a penalty on it`
    `training my employer or the Controller requires`
    `my repatriation`
    `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass`
    `a duplicate pass fee for the first replacement of a lost pass`
    `a duplicate pass fee for a second or later replacement of a lost pass`
    `a salary deduction the Employment Act or my terms of employment allow`
    `a fee a licensed employment agency may lawfully charge me`
    `some other sum`

DECLARE `The circumstances` HAS
    `my pass`                                                IS A `Kind of work pass`
    `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Conditional on an official act: the Controller's permission under s 25(6) and reg 18.
    `if the Controller permits otherwise`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `I consented in writing to bear it`                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What the Act says about it` IS ONE OF
    `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`
    `taking it is an offence`
    `taking it is presumed an offence until the taker proves otherwise`
    `it may lawfully be taken from me`

GIVEN `pass` IS A `Kind of work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 18 lets the Controller shift training and repatriation to me with my consent` IF
    CONSIDER `pass`
    WHEN `a work permit for a domestic worker` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a work permit for other work`        THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `pass` IS A `Kind of work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 17 lists a duplicate fee for my pass` IF
    CONSIDER `pass`
    WHEN `a miscellaneous work pass` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Reg 17 is the fee "prescribed as recoverable" (s 22A(3)(b)): a duplicate fee for a damaged pass or a first lost
-- pass, where I was negligent.
GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Charge`, `c` IS A `The circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fee is prescribed as recoverable from me` IF
        `regulation 17 lists a duplicate fee for my pass` (`c`'s `my pass`)
    AND `c`'s `the damage or loss was caused by my negligence`
    AND CONSIDER `the charge`
        WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass`                       THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for the first replacement of a lost pass` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- INFERENCE: a duplicate pass is an "issuance" of a pass, so its fee is within s 25(6)(a) unless reg 17 makes it
-- recoverable. For training and repatriation under the reg 18 passes, the Controller's permission needs my written
-- consent; for every other s 25(6) charge the Act's "except where the Controller permits otherwise" is enough.
GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Charge`, `c` IS A `The circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my employer must bear the charge` IF
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `work pass application, issue, renewal or reinstatement fees` THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    WHEN `the cost of security the Controller requires`              THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    WHEN `my medical insurance the Controller requires`              THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    WHEN `my medical examinations the Controller requires`           THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    WHEN `the levy or a penalty on it`                               THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    WHEN `training my employer or the Controller requires`           THEN NOT `the Controller has shifted it to me`
    WHEN `my repatriation`                                           THEN NOT `the Controller has shifted it to me`
    WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass`                   THEN NOT (`the fee is prescribed as recoverable from me` `the charge` `c` OR `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`)
    WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for the first replacement of a lost pass` THEN NOT (`the fee is prescribed as recoverable from me` `the charge` `c` OR `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`)
    WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for a second or later replacement of a lost pass` THEN NOT `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
    OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        `the Controller has shifted it to me` MEANS
                `c`'s `if the Controller permits otherwise`
            AND (    NOT `regulation 18 lets the Controller shift training and repatriation to me with my consent` (`c`'s `my pass`)
                 OR  `c`'s `I consented in writing to bear it`)

GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Charge`, `c` IS A `The circumstances`
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it`
`What does the Act say about my employer taking this from me` MEANS
    IF `my employer must bear the charge` `the charge` `c`
    THEN `my employer must bear it, and taking it from me exposes my employer to a financial penalty`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the charge`
         WHEN `a fee for getting the job`                                 THEN `taking it is an offence`
         WHEN `a fee for keeping the job`                                 THEN `taking it is an offence`
         WHEN `a deposit or other financial guarantee for my employment`  THEN `taking it is an offence`
         WHEN `a salary deduction the Employment Act or my terms of employment allow` THEN `it may lawfully be taken from me`
         WHEN `a fee a licensed employment agency may lawfully charge me` THEN `it may lawfully be taken from me`
         OTHERWISE
             -- A fee prescribed as recoverable is outside the presumption (s 22A(3)(b)). Anything else the employer
             -- need not bear -- including a s 25(6) cost the Controller has shifted to me -- is outside s 22A(3)(a)
             -- too, and so on the literal words is presumed to be for my employment (a literal reading; see NOTES.md).
             IF `the fee is prescribed as recoverable from me` `the charge` `c`
             THEN `it may lawfully be taken from me`
             ELSE `taking it is presumed an offence until the taker proves otherwise`

-- Seventh Schedule: a duplicate pass to replace a damaged pass is $65.40 (items 1(e), 2(d), 3(d), 4(c), 8(b)); for the
-- first replacement of a lost pass, $109 (items 1(f), 2(e), 3(e), 4(d), 8(c)).
GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Charge`, `c` IS A `The circumstances`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of a duplicate pass fee can my employer recover from me` MEANS
    IF `the fee is prescribed as recoverable from me` `the charge` `c`
    THEN CONSIDER `the charge`
         WHEN `a duplicate pass fee for a damaged pass` THEN JUST 65.40
         OTHERWISE JUST 109
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 23A(1)(a): on conviction under s 22A(2) the court "shall, in addition to imposing on that person any other
-- punishment, order the person to pay" a sum "equal to the amount of the sum or other benefit ... the person deducted
-- or received in contravention of that section". s 23A(3): the order has effect "as if that sum were a fine". The text
-- does not say the sum is paid to me.
GIVEN `the amount taken from me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`If the taker is convicted, what must the court order the taker to pay` MEANS `the amount taken from me`

§§ `9 -- my employment when my pass is suspended or revoked`

-- s 9(1): where the Controller suspends or revokes the pass, the Controller "must notify the employer" and the
-- employer "must, within 7 days of receiving the notification, terminate the employment of the foreign employee".
-- s 9(3): failure -- "a financial penalty of an amount, not exceeding $10,000". s 9(5): the termination is not to be
-- "capable of negotiation with a trade union", industrial action, "the subject matter of a trade dispute or of
-- conciliation proceedings or any method of redress", or an industrial matter. s 9(6): where s 9(1) is contravened,
-- the employee is not, "by reason only of such contravention, ... deemed to be employed under an illegal contract".
-- Gloss: "revoke" ends the pass for good; "suspend" stops it for a time (s 7(5)(b), (c)).
GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Within how many days of being notified must my employer end my employment` MEANS
    IF `pass`'s `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass`
    THEN JUST 7
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I take the ending of my employment to my union or a trade dispute` IF
    NOT `pass`'s `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass`

-- s 9(1) and s 14(1) as duties with deadlines, counted in days from the notification or the loss.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `my employer`, `me`
DECLARE `Act under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `end my employment`
    `report the loss, destruction or defacement of my work pass to the Controller`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act under the Act`
DECIDE `my employer's duty to end my employment after revocation` IS
    PARTY  `my employer`
    MUST   `end my employment`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `my employer`

§§ `13, 14 -- my work pass in my hands`

-- s 14(1): "When a work pass has been lost, destroyed or defaced, the foreign employee or the employer or the
-- self-employed foreigner (as the case may be) must report to the Controller within 7 days of such loss, destruction or
-- defacement". s 13(1): "A work pass holder must not allow any other person to have possession of his or her work
-- pass." (The punishments are in the s 22 table above.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act under the Act`
DECIDE `my duty to report a lost work pass` IS
    PARTY  `me`
    MUST   `report the loss, destruction or defacement of my work pass to the Controller`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `me`

GIVEN `days after the loss when I reported it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I report my lost work pass in time` IF
    `days after the loss when I reported it` AT MOST 7

§§ `11 -- the levy on my pass`

-- s 11(1): the Minister may by order impose a levy "on employers in respect of any foreign employee ..., or on
-- self-employed foreigners". (2): "The levy continues to be payable unless the work pass -- (a) has expired; (b) has
-- been suspended or revoked by the Controller; or (c) has been cancelled by the Controller on application by the
-- employer." (4), (5): a late-payment penalty "for every day the amount remains unpaid", at a rate set by order, "but
-- the total penalty must not exceed 30% of the amount of levy outstanding".
DECLARE `Who pays the levy` IS ONE OF `my employer`, `I do`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`
GIVETH A `Who pays the levy`
`Who must pay the levy on my work pass` MEANS
    IF `Am I a self-employed foreigner` `me` THEN `I do` ELSE `my employer`

-- My stopping work is not on the s 11(2) list, so it is asked and ignored.
GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`, `I have stopped working` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the levy on my work pass still payable` IF
        `pass`'s `the period specified in the pass has not ended`
    AND NOT `pass`'s `the Controller has suspended or revoked the pass`
    AND NOT `pass`'s `the Controller has cancelled the pass on application`

GIVEN `penalty at the ordered rate` IS A NUMBER, `levy outstanding` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most late-payment penalty I can be charged on unpaid levy` MEANS
    `the lower of` `penalty at the ordered rate` (`levy outstanding` TIMES 30 DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `5(1), (3)-(6), (8), 6, 6A, 22A(2), 22B -- what the person who employs me risks`

-- s 5(1): "A person must not employ a foreign employee unless the foreign employee has a valid work pass." (3): nor
-- "otherwise than in accordance with the conditions of the foreign employee's work pass". (4), (5): not knowing I was a
-- foreigner is no defence "unless the defendant further proves that the defendant had exercised due diligence", and
-- there is none "unless the defendant had checked the passport, document of identity or other travel document".
-- s 5(6): "(a) ... a fine of at least $5,000 and not more than $30,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12
-- months or to both; and (b) on a second or subsequent conviction -- (i) in the case of an individual -- ... a fine of
-- at least $10,000 and not more than $30,000 and with imprisonment for a term of not less than one month and not more
-- than 12 months; or (ii) in any other case -- ... a fine of at least $20,000 and not more than $60,000". (8): s 5(3)
-- -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 6A(1): "An occupier of a work place who has control of access to the work place must not permit any foreigner
-- without a valid work pass to enter or remain at the work place"; (7) "occupier" means "the principal contractor who
-- undertakes any construction works at the work place" and anyone the Minister specifies. (6): "(a) ... $15,000 or
-- ... 12 months or ... both; and (b) on a second or subsequent conviction, ... $30,000 or ... 2 years or ... both".
-- s 22A(2): $30,000 or 2 years or both. s 22B(1): obtaining a pass "for a trade or business that does not exist, that
-- is not in operation or that does not require the employment of such a foreign employee" and failing to employ me --
-- "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not less than 6 months and not more than 2 years" and a fine up to
-- $6,000.
-- Gloss: a "principal contractor" contracts with the owner, developer or lessee to carry out construction works.
DECLARE `Their offence` IS ONE OF
    `employing me without a valid work pass`
    `employing me against the conditions of my work pass`
    `letting me into a construction work place without a valid work pass`
    `taking money from me for my employment`
    `obtaining a work pass for me for a phantom business and not employing me`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Their offence`, `they are an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is their second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Punishment`
`the punishment the Act sets for their offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `employing me without a valid work pass` THEN
        IF NOT `it is their second or subsequent conviction` THEN `a fine from` 5000 30000 0 12
        ELSE IF `they are an individual`                    THEN `a fine from` 10000 30000 1 12
                                                             ELSE `a fine from` 20000 60000 0 0
    WHEN `employing me against the conditions of my work pass` THEN `a fine from` 0 10000 0 0
    WHEN `letting me into a construction work place without a valid work pass` THEN
        IF `it is their second or subsequent conviction` THEN `a fine from` 0 30000 0 24 ELSE `a fine from` 0 15000 0 12
    WHEN `taking money from me for my employment` THEN `a fine from` 0 30000 0 24
    WHEN `obtaining a work pass for me for a phantom business and not employing me` THEN `a fine from` 0 6000 6 24

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Their offence`, `they are an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is their second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the least fine the person who employed me must get` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for their offence` `the offence` `they are an individual` `it is their second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the least fine`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Their offence`, `they are an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is their second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the person who employed me can be fined` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for their offence` `the offence` `they are an individual` `it is their second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the most fine`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Their offence`, `they are an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is their second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the shortest imprisonment the person who employed me must get, in months` MEANS
    (`the punishment the Act sets for their offence` `the offence` `they are an individual` `it is their second or subsequent conviction`)'s `the least months of imprisonment`

-- s 5(9)(b): "all convictions against the same person for the contravention of subsection (1) at one and the same
-- trial shall be deemed to be one conviction".
GIVEN `earlier trials at which they were convicted under section 5(1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would this be their second or subsequent conviction for employing a foreigner without a pass` IF
    `earlier trials at which they were convicted under section 5(1)` AT LEAST 1

GIVEN `they did not know I was a foreigner` IS A BOOLEAN, `they exercised due diligence to find out my nationality` IS A BOOLEAN, `they checked my passport, document of identity or other travel document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the person who employed me rely on not knowing I was a foreigner` IF
    `they did not know I was a foreigner` AND `they exercised due diligence to find out my nationality` AND `they checked my passport, document of identity or other travel document`

-- s 6: "Where a foreigner is found at any premises, the occupier of the premises is presumed, until the contrary is
-- proved, to have employed the foreigner."
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me`, `I am found at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the occupier of the premises where I am found presumed to have employed me` IF
    `Am I a foreigner under the Act` `me` AND `I am found at the premises`

GIVEN `pass` IS A `My work pass`, `they are the principal contractor for construction works there, or specified by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `they control access to the work place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the occupier keep me out of the construction work place` IF
        `they are the principal contractor for construction works there, or specified by the Minister`
    AND `they control access to the work place`
    AND NOT `the pass is still in force` `pass`

-- s 6A(2): if I am found there without a valid pass, the occupier is presumed to have had control of access, to have
-- permitted me and to have known. (3): not knowing I was a foreigner rebuts this only with due diligence "(a) to
-- prevent the foreigner from entering or remaining ...; (b) to ascertain that the person was a citizen ... or
-- permanent resident ... by checking the person's passport ...; or (c) to ascertain that the foreigner had ... a valid
-- work pass by checking his or her original work pass". (4): (a) needs "all reasonable measures ... including all the
-- measures prescribed". INFERENCE: the "or" makes (a), (b) and (c) alternatives.
GIVEN `they did not know I was a foreigner` IS A BOOLEAN, `they took all reasonable and prescribed measures to keep out foreigners without a valid pass` IS A BOOLEAN, `they checked my passport or travel document` IS A BOOLEAN, `they checked my original work pass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the occupier rebut the presumptions by not knowing I was a foreigner` IF
        `they did not know I was a foreigner`
    AND (    `they took all reasonable and prescribed measures to keep out foreigners without a valid pass`
         OR  `they checked my passport or travel document`
         OR  `they checked my original work pass`)

-- s 22B(2): a person "charged with more than 5 offences under subsection (1)" and "convicted of at least 6 of those
-- offences at the same trial" shall be punished "with caning in addition", subject to the Criminal Procedure Code 2010
-- ss 325(1) and 330(1); (3): a person those sections exempt gets instead "a fine not exceeding $10,000". The CPC
-- exemptions are not deposited and are asked as a fact.
DECLARE `The extra punishment` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `caning`
    `a fine of up to 10000 in lieu of caning`

GIVEN `offences charged` IS A NUMBER, `offences convicted at the same trial` IS A NUMBER, `the Criminal Procedure Code exempts them from caning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The extra punishment`
`What extra punishment must the person who obtained phantom passes get` MEANS
    IF `offences charged` GREATER THAN 5 AND `offences convicted at the same trial` AT LEAST 6
    THEN IF `the Criminal Procedure Code exempts them from caning`
         THEN `a fine of up to 10000 in lieu of caning`
         ELSE `caning`
    ELSE `none`

-- The Controller's financial penalties on my employer (prescribed infringements, s 2): s 9(3) not ending my
-- employment within 7 days -- "not exceeding $10,000"; s 25(1) inflating the "foreign employee entitlement" --
-- $20,000; s 25(2) a regulatory condition -- $10,000; s 25(3) an employer who "inadvertently, or without intent to
-- mislead or defraud," gives inaccurate information -- $20,000; s 25(4) taking from me what s 25(6) makes it bear --
-- $20,000; s 25A(2) a prescribed duty -- $10,000.
DECLARE `My employer's infringement` IS ONE OF
    `not ending my employment within 7 days of revocation`
    `inflating its foreign employee entitlement`
    `breaching a regulatory condition`
    `inadvertently giving the Controller inaccurate information`
    `taking from me what it must bear`
    `breaching a prescribed duty`

GIVEN `the infringement` IS A `My employer's infringement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most financial penalty the Controller can impose on my employer for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `not ending my employment within 7 days of revocation`        THEN 10000
    WHEN `inflating its foreign employee entitlement`                  THEN 20000
    WHEN `breaching a regulatory condition`                            THEN 10000
    WHEN `inadvertently giving the Controller inaccurate information` THEN 20000
    WHEN `taking from me what it must bear`                            THEN 20000
    WHEN `breaching a prescribed duty`                                 THEN 10000

§§ `25(2), 25A, 25C, 25G -- the Controller's financial penalties on me, and my appeal`

-- s 25(2)(b): where a foreign employee "to whom a work pass applies or had applied" fails to comply with "any
-- regulatory condition of the work pass", the Controller may impose "a financial penalty of an amount, not exceeding
-- $10,000". s 25A(2): failing a duty prescribed after in-principle approval -- "not exceeding $10,000".
-- s 25C(4)(c): in proceedings before the Controller "no party may be represented by an advocate or solicitor or a paid
-- agent". s 25G(1): an appeal "must be lodged within 14 days after the receipt of the determination or direction".
-- (3): an appeal "does not suspend the effect of the determination or direction ... unless the appeal is against the
-- imposition, or the amount, of a financial penalty".
-- Gloss: a "financial penalty" is imposed by the Controller, not a court; it is not a conviction. A "regulatory
-- condition" is a pass condition prescribed or imposed as such (s 2).
DECLARE `My infringement` IS ONE OF
    `breaching a regulatory condition of my work pass`
    `breaching a duty prescribed after in-principle approval`

GIVEN `the infringement` IS A `My infringement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most financial penalty the Controller can impose on me for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the infringement`
    WHEN `breaching a regulatory condition of my work pass`        THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching a duty prescribed after in-principle approval` THEN 10000

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be represented by a lawyer or paid agent before the Controller` IF FALSE

GIVEN `days after I received the determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my appeal to the Appeal Board in time` IF
    `days after I received the determination` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `my appeal is against the imposition or amount of a financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my appeal hold off the Controller's determination` IF
    `my appeal is against the imposition or amount of a financial penalty`
